{
  "iri": "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0006915",
  "lang": "en",
  "description": [
    "A programmed cell death process which begins when a cell receives an internal (e.g. DNA damage) or external signal (e.g. an extracellular death ligand), and proceeds through a series of biochemical events (signaling pathway phase) which trigger an execution phase."
  ],
  "synonyms": [
    "apoptosis",
    "apoptotic cell death",
    "programmed cell death by apoptosis",
    "cell suicide"
  ],
  "annotation": {
    "comment": [
      "Note that a caspase-independent apoptotic process is also recognized in certain biological contexts."
    ],
